@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
<p class="text-muted">Last updated: May 2026</p>

<p>
    This is a class project built for CIS-560. It is not a production application and is not intended for real public use.
</p>

<h4>What We Collect</h4>
<p>
    When you register as a library member, we collect your first name, last name, email address, and a hashed version of your password.
    Your password is never stored in plain text — only a one-way hash is kept, which means we cannot see or recover the original password.
</p>

<h4>What We Track</h4>
<p>
    When you check out a book, we record which book copy you borrowed, when it was checked out, and when it is due.
    When you return a book, we record the return date and the condition you reported.
    This information is used to manage the library's inventory and is visible to library staff.
</p>

<h4>Who Sees Your Data</h4>
<p>
    Your personal information and checkout history are accessible to library staff (administrators) for the purpose
    of operating the library. Other library members cannot see your information or checkout history.
</p>

<h4>How Long We Keep It</h4>
<p>
    Member records and checkout history are kept indefinitely as part of the library's records.
    You may contact a librarian to request that your account be removed.
</p>

<h4>Cookies</h4>
<p>
    We use a single authentication cookie to keep you logged in after you sign in. This cookie does not track you across other websites.
    Logging out clears the cookie.
</p>

<h4>Disclaimer</h4>
<p>
    Since this is a student project, no real personal data should be entered. Use a fake name and a non-personal email address.
    Do not reuse a password that you use anywhere else.
</p>

<h4>Questions</h4>
<p>
    For questions about this project or its privacy practices, please contact the project team.
</p>